### DAG Dependency Chain

```
Stage Land
    │
    ▼
Raw CDC Merge (PSG)
    │
    ▼
Conformed DWH Incremental (BIW_DWH)
    │
    ▼
Feature Snapshot Generation (PFS / PFUS)
    │
    ▼
Data Quality Assertions (dbt tests)
    │
    ▼
Outbound View Refresh (OUT layer)
    │
    ▼
SLA Sensor Alert (if > 4:30 AM threshold)
```

### dbt Incremental Model Pattern

```sql
-- models/mart/fct_sales_transaction_plu_atm.sql
{{
  config(
    materialized  = 'incremental',
    unique_key    = 'SALES_TXN_KEY',
    incremental_strategy = 'merge',
    on_schema_change = 'append_new_columns'
  )
}}

SELECT
    {{ dbt_utils.generate_surrogate_key(['STORE_KEY','PLU_KEY','TXN_DATE','TXN_TIME']) }}
        AS SALES_TXN_KEY,
    STORE_KEY,
    PLU_KEY,
    TXN_DATE,
    SALES_QTY_AMT,
    SALES_RETAIL_AMT,
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()  AS CDW_RECD_LOAD_DT,
    {{ var('CDW_PROCESS_KEY') }} AS CDW_PROCESS_KEY
FROM {{ ref('wrk_sales_transaction_dedup') }}

{% if is_incremental() %}
WHERE CDW_PROCESS_KEY > (
    SELECT MAX(CDW_PROCESS_KEY)
    FROM {{ this }}
)
{% endif %}
```

### 🗣️ Spoken Voice Track

> *"Our ingestion and processing pipeline leverages a dbt-on-Snowflake architecture orchestrated by Airflow and Control-M:*
>
> **1. Incremental Loading & Merge Strategy:** For high-volume transaction facts, we use dbt's incremental materialization with a merge strategy. We filter incoming records using an operational watermark on `CDW_PROCESS_KEY`, ensuring we only process modified or newly landed records.
>
> **2. Handling Out-of-Order CDC:** In the intermediate WRK layer, we apply Snowflake's `QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY NATURAL_KEY ORDER BY SOURCE_TIMESTAMP DESC) = 1` to guarantee that out-of-order change events are deduplicated before updating target tables.
>
> **3. DAG Orchestration & SLA Sensors:** Our orchestration DAG enforces strict task dependency chains from Stage Land through to Outbound View Refresh. We embed SLA sensors that alert on-call engineering teams if upstream stages delay beyond 4:30 AM."*

