## 6. Stage 5 — Security, Governance & Data Quality

> **Interviewer Question:**
> *"How do you handle RBAC security, data masking, and testing?"*

### Snowflake RBAC Role Matrix

| Role | Schema Access | Permissions |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `BIW_TRANSFORMER_ROLE` | `STG`, `PSG`, `WRK`, `BIW_DWH` | Write (INSERT, MERGE, DELETE) |
| `BIW_ANALYST_ROLE` | `OUT` views only | Read-only SELECT |
| `BIW_ADMIN_ROLE` | All schemas | Full DDL + DML |
| `ML_FEATURE_ROLE` | `OUT`, `BIW_DWH` | Read-only SELECT on feature tables |

### dbt Data Quality Test Tiers

```yaml
# models/mart/schema.yml
models:
  - name: fct_sales_transaction_plu_atm
    description: "Atomic PLU-level sales transaction fact table"
    columns:
      - name: SALES_TXN_KEY
        tests:
          - unique
          - not_null
      - name: STORE_KEY
        tests:
          - not_null
          - relationships:
              to: ref('dim_org_loc')
              field: LOC_KEY
      - name: SALES_QTY_AMT
        tests:
          - dbt_utils.expression_is_true:
              expression: ">= 0"
      - name: SALES_RETAIL_AMT
        tests:
          - dbt_utils.expression_is_true:
              expression: ">= 0"
```

### 🗣️ Spoken Voice Track

> *"Security, governance, and data quality were built into the pipeline design from day one:*
>
> **1. Snowflake RBAC & Security:** We implemented functional role separation. Pipeline execution runs under `BIW_TRANSFORMER_ROLE` with write access restricted strictly to staging and warehouse schemas. Business analysts query via `BIW_ANALYST_ROLE` with read-only access limited to the consumer views layer. Dynamic Data Masking policies mask sensitive supplier cost attributes for unauthorized roles.*
