## 8. Databricks Feature Store & Delta Lake Deep Dive

> **Interviewer Question:**
> *"Walk me through how you built the Databricks Feature Store for demand forecasting."*

### Databricks Feature Store Architecture

```
Azure ADLS (Raw Delta Bronze Layer)
        │
        ▼
Databricks Bronze → Silver Pipeline (PySpark CDC Merge)
        │
        ▼
Silver Delta Tables (Cleansed, Conformed)
        │
        ▼
Gold Feature Engineering Jobs (PySpark)
  ├── Rolling 4-week sales aggregations
  ├── Price elasticity window features
  ├── Promotional indicator flags
  └── Range status point-in-time features
        │
        ▼
Databricks Feature Store (Unity Catalog)
  ├── fs.create_table("pfs.item_loc_features")
  ├── Offline Store → ML Training (time-travel PIT lookup)
  └── Online Store → Real-time model inference
        │
        ▼
MLflow Model Registry → Relex / Advanced Analytics Forecast Engines
```

### PySpark Point-in-Time Feature Job

```python
from databricks.feature_store import FeatureStoreClient
from pyspark.sql import functions as F
from pyspark.sql.window import Window

fs = FeatureStoreClient()

# Step 1: Load Silver Delta table with time travel for PIT integrity
silver_df = spark.read.format("delta") \
    .option("timestampAsOf", training_cutoff_date) \
    .load("/mnt/silver/product_range")

# Step 2: Compute rolling features
window_4wk = Window.partitionBy("ITEM_KEY", "LOC_KEY") \
    .orderBy("EVENT_DATE") \
    .rowsBetween(-28, -1)

features_df = silver_df \
    .withColumn("SALES_ROLL_4WK_AVG",
        F.avg("SALES_QTY_AMT").over(window_4wk)) \
    .withColumn("PROMO_WEEKS_ROLL_4WK",
        F.sum("IS_ON_PROMO_FLG").over(window_4wk)) \
    .withColumn("PRICE_CHANGE_FLG",
        F.when(F.col("CURR_PRICE_AMT") != F.lag("CURR_PRICE_AMT", 1)
        .over(Window.partitionBy("ITEM_KEY","LOC_KEY")
        .orderBy("EVENT_DATE")), 1).otherwise(0))

# Step 3: Write to Databricks Feature Store
fs.write_table(
    name       = "pfs.item_loc_daily_features",
    df         = features_df,
    mode       = "merge"
)
```

### Delta Lake Time Travel for PIT Lookups

```python
# Query feature state as of specific training date — prevents data leakage
historical_features = spark.read.format("delta") \
    .option("timestampAsOf", "2025-06-01T00:00:00") \
    .table("pfs.item_loc_daily_features")

# Or by version number
historical_features = spark.read.format("delta") \
    .option("versionAsOf", 42) \
    .table("pfs.item_loc_daily_features")
```

### 🗣️ Spoken Voice Track

> *"Our Databricks Feature Store follows a Medallion Architecture pattern — Bronze, Silver, Gold — built on Delta Lake with Unity Catalog governance:*
>
> *Bronze tables receive raw CDC events from Azure ADLS. Silver tables apply cleansing, deduplication, and schema enforcement. Gold feature jobs run complex PySpark transformations — rolling sales aggregations, promotional indicator windows, and price elasticity calculations.*
>
> *The key engineering challenge was Point-in-Time correctness. For ML model training, we must guarantee that features used to train on a historical date reflect only information that was available on that date — no future data can leak in. Delta Lake's time-travel capability — using `timestampAsOf` or `versionAsOf` — gives us this guarantee natively. We simply read the feature table at the training cutoff timestamp and join it against our event spine.*
>
> *Features are registered in the Databricks Feature Store under Unity Catalog, which gives us a single governance layer for ACLs, data lineage, and audit logs across all feature tables."*

