## 9. Lakehouse vs Data Warehouse — When Interviewers Ask

> **Interviewer Question:**
> *"Everyone is talking about Lakehouse — what is it and how does it compare to a Data Warehouse?"*

### Comparison Table

| Dimension | Data Warehouse (Snowflake) | Data Lakehouse (Databricks + Delta Lake) |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **Primary Workload** | BI, Reporting, SQL Analytics | ML Feature Engineering, Model Training |
| **Data Format** | Structured tables, Parquet-backed | Delta Lake (Parquet + Transaction Log) |
| **Schema Approach** | Schema-on-Write (strict) | Schema-on-Read + Schema Enforcement |
| **ACID Transactions** | Native | Delta Lake provides ACID on object storage |
| **History / Time-Travel** | Snowflake Time Travel (90 days) | Delta Time Travel (version or timestamp) |
| **Compute Model** | Snowflake Virtual Warehouses | Databricks Spark Clusters / Serverless SQL |
| **Best For** | Governed BI dashboards, conformed dims | Distributed ML feature pipelines, streaming |
| **Our Usage** | BIW_DWH Kimball Star Schemas, OUT views | PFS/PFUS Feature Store, PIT Feature Joins |

### Medallion Architecture Mapping to Our Schema

```
Bronze  =  EDL + STG  (raw landing, schema-on-read)
Silver  =  PSG + WRK  (cleansed CDC, deduplicated)
Gold    =  BIW_DWH + OUT  (conformed Kimball + consumer views)
```

### 🗣️ Spoken Voice Track

> *"A Lakehouse combines the cost efficiency and flexibility of a Data Lake with the reliability, ACID semantics, and query performance traditionally associated with a Data Warehouse.*
>
> *In practice, I've worked with this pattern directly. Our Databricks platform uses Delta Lake as the storage format — giving us versioned, ACID-compliant tables on top of Azure Blob Storage. This means we get time-travel queries, schema enforcement and evolution, and unified batch and streaming on the same Delta table.*
>
> *In our architecture, we deliberately use both platforms for their strengths. Databricks Lakehouse handles heavy feature engineering, ML training pipelines, and raw data persistence. Snowflake Data Warehouse handles conformed Kimball models, BI consumption, and governed enterprise reporting.*
>
> *The key engineering challenge I solved was building the synchronization and consistency layer between them so both platforms share the same source of truth."*

